            <ArticleTitle>Pituitary secretions and wake-sleep cycle.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>42-53</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Neurohumoral correlations of sleep are considered from three aspects: 1. Metabolism and cerebral blood circulation (CBF, EEG, endocranial pressure, cerebral temperature); 2. Neuromediators and neuropeptides (5-HT, hypnogen neuropeptides); 3. The influence of the sleeping-waking cycle on adeno-hypophyseal secretion rhythms (GH, PRL, LH, TSH). Variations of these parameters can play an important role in the onset of night crises of migraine and cluster headache.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
